  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Trajectory plot\n",
    "\n",
    "Colored by time; any long untracked stretch is drawn as a gap in the line rather than a\n",
    "straight-line guess, so you can see directly where and for how long tracking was lost.\n"
   ],
   "id": "cf00a7909071eec"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-09-10T23:14:09.490212Z",
     "start_time": "2026-09-10T23:14:09.332668Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plot_trajectory(\n",
    "    df,\n",
    "    title=Path(CSV_PATH).stem,\n",
    "    dish_center_mm=DISH_CENTER_MM,\n",
    "    dish_radius_mm=DISH_RADIUS_MM,\n",
    ")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ],
   "id": "a94c89722e067651",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 600x600 with 2 Axes>"
      ],
      "image/png": ""
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data",
     "jetTransient": {
      "display_id": null
     }
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 134
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Speed over time (per-epoch)\n",
    "\n",
    "A single global max speed is very sensitive to one noisy frame, so this breaks the video into\n",
    "fixed-length epochs and reports max/mean/median speed per epoch — useful for seeing when the\n",
    "larva was moving vs. resting.\n"
   ],
   "id": "c4f2a535519349d9"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-09-10T23:14:09.550819Z",
     "start_time": "2026-09-10T23:14:09.538548Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "EPOCH_S = 10  # seconds per epoch\n",
    "\n",
    "epoch_stats = summarize_by_epoch(df, epoch_s=EPOCH_S)\n",
    "epoch_stats\n"
   ],
   "id": "165291a2965ff797",
